IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgo-penalties`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 12 Division 1, the middle: privileged communications (s 393), the form of company records (s 395),
-- the duty to take precautions against falsification (s 396), inspection of records (s 396A), accounts not kept (s 396B), translations (s 397)
-- and the certificate of incorporation (s 398). Part agent sgo.
--
-- A duty whose "where" or "if" is unmet (the subsection does not reach the case) answers NOTHING, not JUST FALSE: JUST FALSE would say the duty
-- has been broken. Each such site is a fork line (NOTES.md, "a duty whose if or where is unmet", one of the six open questions of 2026-11-05).
-- The penalty of each offence is a `Penalty` (sg-core.l4); the "officer in default" is s 408(3), in sgo-penalties.l4.

§ `Section 393: privileged communications`

-- Named as the bar, as the guide asks. JUST TRUE = the inspector is barred; JUST FALSE = the exception for the name and address of the client;
-- NOTHING = the section does not speak (not an inspector, or not a privileged communication).
-- src:27585 | 393. No inspector appointed under this Act may require disclosure
-- src:27586 | by a solicitor of any privileged communication made to the solicitor
-- src:27587 | in that capacity, except as respects the name and address of the
-- src:27588 | solicitor’s client.
@ref s 393 (src:27585-27588)
GIVEN `the person requiring disclosure is an inspector appointed under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is a privileged communication made to the solicitor in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is the name or address of the solicitor's client` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 393 the inspector is barred from requiring disclosure by the solicitor` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person requiring disclosure is an inspector appointed under this Act` AND `the information is a privileged communication made to the solicitor in that capacity`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No inspector appointed under this Act may require disclosure by a solicitor of any privileged communication made to the solicitor in that capacity"
    ELSE (IF `the information is the name or address of the solicitor's client`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except as respects the name and address of the solicitor's client" (an "except" once met: the bar does not apply to the name and address; fork F-393-1)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

§ `Section 395: form of company records`

§§ `Section 395(4): the words used in sections 395, 396 and 396A`

-- src:27637 | (4) In this section and sections 396 and 396A —
-- src:27639 | “company” includes a corporation which is required to keep
-- src:27640 | company records under this Act;
@ref s 395(4) (src:27637-27640)
GIVEN `the term is used in section 395, 396 or 396A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is required to keep company records under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(4) "company" the corporation is within the word company` MEANS
    IF NOT `the term is used in section 395, 396 or 396A`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In this section and sections 396 and 396A"
    ELSE (IF `the corporation is required to keep company records under this Act`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "\"company\" includes a corporation which is required to keep company records under this Act"

-- src:27642 | “company record” means any register, index, minute book,
-- src:27643 | accounting record, minute or other document required by this
-- src:27644 | Act to be kept by a company;
@ref s 395(4) 27637 (src:27642-27644)
GIVEN `the term is used in section 395, 396 or 396A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a register, index, minute book, accounting record, minute or other document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is required by this Act to be kept by a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(4) "company record" the thing is a company record` MEANS
    IF NOT `the term is used in section 395, 396 or 396A`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In this section and sections 396 and 396A"
    ELSE (IF `the thing is a register, index, minute book, accounting record, minute or other document` AND `the thing is required by this Act to be kept by a company`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"company record\" means any register, index, minute book, accounting record, minute or other document required by this Act to be kept by a company"

-- src:27646 | “in electronic form” means in the form of an electronic record as
-- src:27647 | defined in section 2(1) of the Electronic Transactions
-- src:27648 | Act 2010;
@ref s 395(4) 27637 (src:27646-27648)
GIVEN `the term is used in section 395, 396 or 396A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record is in the form of an electronic record as defined in section 2(1) of the Electronic Transactions Act 2010` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(4) "in electronic form" the record is in electronic form` MEANS
    IF NOT `the term is used in section 395, 396 or 396A`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In this section and sections 396 and 396A"
    ELSE (IF `the record is in the form of an electronic record as defined in section 2(1) of the Electronic Transactions Act 2010`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"in electronic form\" means in the form of an electronic record as defined in section 2(1) of the Electronic Transactions Act 2010"

-- src:27650 | “in hard copy form” means in a paper form or similar form
-- src:27651 | capable of being read.
@ref s 395(4) 27637 (src:27650-27651)
GIVEN `the term is used in section 395, 396 or 396A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record is in a paper form or similar form capable of being read` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(4) "in hard copy form" the record is in hard copy form` MEANS
    IF NOT `the term is used in section 395, 396 or 396A`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In this section and sections 396 and 396A"
    ELSE (IF `the record is in a paper form or similar form capable of being read`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"in hard copy form\" means in a paper form or similar form capable of being read"

§§ `Section 395(1) to (3): recording, keeping and reproducing company records`

DECLARE `s 395 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 395(1) adequately record for future reference the information required to be contained in the company records`
    `s 395(3) ensure that the company records kept in electronic form are capable of being reproduced in hard copy form`

-- src:27614 | 395.—(1) A company must adequately record for future reference
-- src:27615 | the information required to be contained in any company records.
@ref s 395(1) (src:27614-27615)
GIVEN `the information required to be contained in the company records has been adequately recorded for future reference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(1) the company has adequately recorded for future reference the information required to be contained in its company records` MEANS
    IF `the information required to be contained in the company records has been adequately recorded for future reference`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must adequately record for future reference the information required to be contained in any company records" (a duty: the provision's own question)

@ref s 395(1) (src:27614-27615)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 395 act`
`s 395(1) a company must adequately record the information required to be contained in its company records` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 395(1) adequately record for future reference the information required to be contained in the company records`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:27619 | (2) Subject to subsection (1), company records may be —
-- src:27621 | (a) kept in hard copy form or in electronic form; and
-- src:27623 | (b) arranged in the manner that the directors of the company
-- src:27624 | think fit.
@ref s 395(2) (src:27619-27624)
GIVEN `the company has complied with section 395(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company records are kept in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company records are kept in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(2)(a) the company records may be kept in that form` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company has complied with section 395(1)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (1), company records may be"; where subsection (1) is not complied with, that subsection governs
    ELSE (IF `the company records are kept in hard copy form` OR `the company records are kept in electronic form`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "(a) kept in hard copy form or in electronic form" does not say "only"

@ref s 395(2) (src:27619-27624)
GIVEN `the company has complied with section 395(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company records are arranged in the manner that the directors of the company think fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(2)(b) the company records may be arranged in that manner` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company has complied with section 395(1)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (1), company records may be"
    ELSE (IF `the company records are arranged in the manner that the directors of the company think fit`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) arranged in the manner that the directors of the company think fit"

-- src:27631 | (3) If company records are kept in electronic form, the company
-- src:27632 | must ensure that they are capable of being reproduced in hard copy
-- src:27633 | form.
@ref s 395(3) (src:27631-27633)
GIVEN `the company records are kept in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has ensured that the company records are capable of being reproduced in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(3) the company has ensured that its company records are capable of being reproduced in hard copy form` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company records are kept in electronic form`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If company records are kept in electronic form"; the duty does not reach records kept in another form (fork F-395-3: a duty whose "if" is unmet)
    ELSE (IF `the company has ensured that the company records are capable of being reproduced in hard copy form`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must ensure that they are capable of being reproduced in hard copy form" (a duty: the provision's own question)

@ref s 395(3) (src:27631-27633)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 395 act`
`s 395(3) a company that keeps records in electronic form must ensure they can be reproduced in hard copy form` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 395(3) ensure that the company records kept in electronic form are capable of being reproduced in hard copy form`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Section 396: duty to take precautions against falsification`

DECLARE `s 396 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 396(2) provide for the manner by which the electronic records are to be authenticated and verified`
    `s 396(3) make default in complying with section 396(1) or (2)`

-- src:27657 | 396.—(1) Where company records are kept otherwise than in hard
-- src:27658 | copy form, reasonable precautions must be taken for —
-- src:27660 | (a) ensuring the proper maintenance and authenticity of the
-- src:27661 | company records;
-- src:27663 | (b) guarding against falsification; and
-- src:27665 | (c) facilitating the discovery of any falsifications.
@ref s 396(1) (src:27657-27665)
GIVEN `the company records are kept otherwise than in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable precautions have been taken for ensuring the proper maintenance and authenticity of the company records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable precautions have been taken for guarding against falsification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable precautions have been taken for facilitating the discovery of any falsifications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396(1) the reasonable precautions that the subsection requires have been taken` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company records are kept otherwise than in hard copy form`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where company records are kept otherwise than in hard copy form"; the subsection does not reach hard copy records (fork F-396-1: a duty whose "where" is unmet)
    ELSE (IF    `reasonable precautions have been taken for ensuring the proper maintenance and authenticity of the company records`
             AND `reasonable precautions have been taken for guarding against falsification`
             AND `reasonable precautions have been taken for facilitating the discovery of any falsifications`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "reasonable precautions must be taken for (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ..." (a duty: the provision's own question)

-- src:27669 | (2) In the case where company records are kept in electronic form,
-- src:27670 | the company must provide for the manner by which the records are to
-- src:27671 | be authenticated and verified.
@ref s 396(2) (src:27669-27671)
GIVEN `the company records are kept in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has provided for the manner by which the records are to be authenticated and verified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396(2) the company has provided for the manner by which the electronic records are to be authenticated and verified` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company records are kept in electronic form`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case where company records are kept in electronic form" (fork F-396-1)
    ELSE (IF `the company has provided for the manner by which the records are to be authenticated and verified`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must provide for the manner by which the records are to be authenticated and verified" (a duty)

@ref s 396(2) (src:27669-27671)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 396 act`
`s 396(2) a company that keeps records in electronic form must provide for how they are authenticated and verified` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 396(2) provide for the manner by which the electronic records are to be authenticated and verified`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:27675 | (3) Where default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (2),
-- src:27676 | the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall
-- src:27677 | each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a
-- src:27678 | fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 396(3) (src:27675-27678)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 396(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396(3) the company is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 396(1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Where default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (2), the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence" says nothing of a company that has made no default; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

@ref s 396(3) (src:27675-27678)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 396(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is guilty of the offence knowingly and wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396(3) the officer of the company is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 396(1) or (2)` AND `s 408(3) the officer is an officer who is in default` `the officer is guilty of the offence knowingly and wilfully` `the officer knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the commission of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "every officer of the company who is in default"; an officer who is not "in default" within s 408(3), or where no default is made, is not spoken of; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

@ref s 396(3) (src:27675-27678)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under section 396(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 396(3) the highest penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under section 396(3)`
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 1000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also a default penalty
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the penalty is that of a person guilty of the offence

@ref s 396(3) (src:27675-27678)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 396 act`
`s 396(3) a company must not make default in taking the precautions` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 396(3) make default in complying with section 396(1) or (2)`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company made default in complying with section 396(1) or (2)"

§ `Section 396A: inspection of records`

DECLARE `s 396A(2) form of inspection` IS ONE OF
    `s 396A(2)(a) a reproduction of the recording, or the relevant part of the recording, in hard copy form`
    `s 396A(2)(b) the recording, or the relevant part of the recording, by electronic means`

DECLARE `s 396A act` IS ONE OF
    `s 396A(1) make the company record available for inspection at the place where it is kept during the hours in which the registered office is accessible to the public`
    `s 396A(4) make default in providing proper facilities for the inspection of company records kept in electronic form`

-- src:27687 | 396A.—(1) Any company record which is by this Act required to
-- src:27688 | be available for inspection must, subject to and in accordance with
-- src:27689 | this Act, be available for inspection at the place where in accordance
-- src:27690 | with this Act it is kept during the hours in which the registered office
-- src:27691 | of the company is accessible to the public.
@ref s 396A(1) (src:27687-27691)
GIVEN `the company record is required by this Act to be available for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspection is at the place where in accordance with this Act the company record is kept` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time is within the hours in which the registered office of the company is accessible to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396A(1) the company must make the company record available for inspection at that place and time` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company record is required by this Act to be available for inspection`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any company record which is by this Act required to be available for inspection"
    ELSE (IF `the inspection is at the place where in accordance with this Act the company record is kept` AND `the time is within the hours in which the registered office of the company is accessible to the public`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must ... be available for inspection at the place where in accordance with this Act it is kept during the hours in which the registered office of the company is accessible to the public"

@ref s 396A(1) (src:27687-27691)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 396A act`
`s 396A(1) a company must make a company record required to be available for inspection available at the place and hours` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 396A(1) make the company record available for inspection at the place where it is kept during the hours in which the registered office is accessible to the public`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:27695 | (2) If company records are kept by the company by recording the
-- src:27696 | information in question in electronic form, any duty imposed on the
-- src:27697 | company under subsection (1) or any other provision of this Act to
-- src:27698 | allow inspection of the company records is to be regarded as a duty to
-- src:27699 | allow inspection of —
-- src:27701 | (a) a reproduction of the recording, or the relevant part of the
-- src:27702 | recording, in hard copy form; or
-- src:27704 | (b) if requested by the person inspecting the recording, the
-- src:27705 | recording, or the relevant part of the recording, by
-- src:27706 | electronic means.
@ref s 396A(2) (src:27695-27706)
GIVEN `the company records are kept by the company by recording the information in question in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person inspecting has requested inspection of the recording by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
      form IS A `s 396A(2) form of inspection`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396A(2) the duty to allow inspection is a duty to allow inspection in that form` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company records are kept by the company by recording the information in question in electronic form`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If company records are kept by the company by recording the information in question in electronic form"
    ELSE CONSIDER form
         WHEN `s 396A(2)(a) a reproduction of the recording, or the relevant part of the recording, in hard copy form` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 396A(2)(b) the recording, or the relevant part of the recording, by electronic means` THEN
             (IF `the person inspecting has requested inspection of the recording by electronic means`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) if requested by the person inspecting, the recording ... by electronic means"

-- src:27710 | (3) Any person permitted by this Act to inspect any company
-- src:27711 | records may make copies of or take extracts from it.
@ref s 396A(3) (src:27710-27711)
GIVEN `the person is permitted by this Act to inspect the company records` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396A(3) the person may make copies of or take extracts from the company records` MEANS
    IF `the person is permitted by this Act to inspect the company records`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person permitted by this Act to inspect any company records"

-- src:27715 | (4) Where company records are kept by the company by recording
-- src:27716 | the information in question in electronic form, the company must
-- src:27717 | ensure that proper facilities are provided to enable the company
-- src:27718 | records to be inspected, and where default is made in complying with
-- src:27719 | this subsection, the company and every officer of the company who is
-- src:27720 | in default shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on
-- src:27721 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a default
-- src:27722 | penalty.
@ref s 396A(4) (src:27715-27722)
GIVEN `the company records are kept by the company by recording the information in question in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has ensured that proper facilities are provided to enable the company records to be inspected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396A(4) the company has ensured that proper facilities are provided to enable the company records to be inspected` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company records are kept by the company by recording the information in question in electronic form`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where company records are kept by the company by recording the information in question in electronic form" (fork F-396-1: a duty whose "where" is unmet)
    ELSE (IF `the company has ensured that proper facilities are provided to enable the company records to be inspected`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must ensure that proper facilities are provided" (a duty)

@ref s 396A(4) (src:27715-27722)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 396A(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396A(4) the company is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 396A(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "where default is made in complying with this subsection, the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence"; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

@ref s 396A(4) (src:27715-27722)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 396A(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is guilty of the offence knowingly and wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396A(4) the officer of the company is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 396A(4)` AND `s 408(3) the officer is an officer who is in default` `the officer is guilty of the offence knowingly and wilfully` `the officer knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the commission of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "every officer of the company who is in default"; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

@ref s 396A(4) (src:27715-27722)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under section 396A(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 396A(4) the highest penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under section 396A(4)`
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 1000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also a default penalty
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the penalty is that of a person guilty of the offence

@ref s 396A(4) (src:27715-27722)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 396A act`
`s 396A(4) a company must not make default in providing proper facilities for inspection` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 396A(4) make default in providing proper facilities for the inspection of company records kept in electronic form`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company made default in providing proper facilities for the inspection of company records kept in electronic form"

§ `Section 396B: liability where proper accounts are not kept`

§§ `Section 396B(1): the period, the offence, the penalty`

-- "the shorter of (a) the period of 2 years immediately preceding the commencement of the investigation; or (b) the period between the incorporation of the company
-- and the commencement of the investigation": the period starts on the later of the two first days. (a) ends on the day before the investigation begins, sg-periods P10.
-- src:27728 | 396B.—(1) If, on an investigation under this Act, it is shown that
-- src:27729 | proper books of account were not kept by the company throughout the
-- src:27730 | shorter of —
-- src:27735 | (a) the period of 2 years immediately preceding the
-- src:27736 | commencement of the investigation; or
-- src:27738 | (b) the period between the incorporation of the company and
-- src:27739 | the commencement of the investigation,
@ref s 396B(1) (src:27728-27739)
GIVEN `the day the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the day the investigation commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 396B(1) the first day of the period throughout which proper books of account must have been kept` MEANS
    IF `the day the company was incorporated` GREATER THAN `period: the first day of a period ending with` (`the day the investigation commenced` MINUS 1) 2 Years
    THEN `the day the company was incorporated`
    ELSE `period: the first day of a period ending with` (`the day the investigation commenced` MINUS 1) 2 Years

-- src:27728 | 396B.—(1) If, on an investigation under this Act, it is shown that
-- src:27729 | proper books of account were not kept by the company throughout the
-- src:27730 | shorter of —
-- src:27735 | (a) the period of 2 years immediately preceding the
-- src:27736 | commencement of the investigation; or
-- src:27738 | (b) the period between the incorporation of the company and
-- src:27739 | the commencement of the investigation,
-- src:27741 | every officer who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and shall
-- src:27742 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to
-- src:27743 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months.
@ref s 396B(1) (src:27728-27743)
GIVEN `an investigation is made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is shown that proper books of account were not kept by the company throughout the shorter of the two periods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is guilty of the offence knowingly and wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396B(1) the officer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF    `an investigation is made under this Act`
       AND `it is shown that proper books of account were not kept by the company throughout the shorter of the two periods`
       AND `s 408(3) the officer is an officer who is in default` `the officer is guilty of the offence knowingly and wilfully` `the officer knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the commission of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "If, on an investigation under this Act, it is shown that proper books of account were not kept ... every officer who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" says nothing of an officer for whom an element fails; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

@ref s 396B(1) (src:27728-27743)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under section 396B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 396B(1) the highest penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under section 396B(1)`
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 5000, 12, FALSE, FALSE)   -- a fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months (not both: the text says "or", not "or to both")
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the penalty is that of a person guilty of the offence

-- src:27747 | (2) Where a person is charged with an offence under subsection (1),
-- src:27748 | it is a defence for the person charged to prove that the person acted
-- src:27749 | honestly and to show that, in the circumstances in which the business
-- src:27750 | of the company was carried on, the default was excusable.
@ref s 396B(2) (src:27747-27750)
GIVEN `the person charged proves that the person acted honestly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person charged shows that, in the circumstances in which the business of the company was carried on, the default was excusable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396B(2) this section gives a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF `the person charged proves that the person acted honestly` AND `the person charged shows that, in the circumstances in which the business of the company was carried on, the default was excusable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence for the person charged to prove that the person acted honestly and to show that ... the default was excusable"; "this section gives no defence on these facts" (the ruling of 2026-11-05 on defences, item (b))

-- src:27754 | (3) For the purposes of this section, proper books of account are
-- src:27755 | deemed not to have been kept in the case of a company —
-- src:27757 | (a) if there have not been kept such books or accounts as are
-- src:27758 | necessary to exhibit and explain the transactions and
-- src:27759 | financial position of the trade or business of the company,
-- src:27760 | including books containing entries from day to day in
-- src:27761 | sufficient detail of all cash received and cash paid, and,
-- src:27762 | where the trade or business has involved dealings in goods,
-- src:27763 | statements of the annual stocktakings and (except in the
-- src:27764 | case of goods sold by way of ordinary retail trade) of all
-- src:27765 | goods sold and purchased, showing the goods and the
-- src:27766 | buyers and sellers of the goods in sufficient detail to enable
-- src:27767 | those goods and those buyers and sellers to be identified; or
-- src:27769 | (b) if such books or accounts have not been kept in such
-- src:27770 | manner as to enable them to be conveniently and properly
-- src:27771 | audited, whether or not the company has appointed an
-- src:27772 | auditor.
@ref s 396B(3) (src:27754-27772)
GIVEN `books or accounts necessary to exhibit and explain the transactions and financial position of the trade or business of the company have been kept` IS A BOOLEAN
      `books containing entries from day to day in sufficient detail of all cash received and cash paid have been kept` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trade or business has involved dealings in goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `statements of the annual stocktakings have been kept` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods were sold by way of ordinary retail trade` IS A BOOLEAN
      `statements of all goods sold and purchased, showing the goods and the buyers and sellers in sufficient detail to enable them to be identified, have been kept` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the books or accounts have been kept in such manner as to enable them to be conveniently and properly audited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396B(3) proper books of account are deemed not to have been kept` MEANS
    IF (NOT necessaryBooksKept) OR (NOT auditable)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "proper books of account are deemed not to have been kept ... (a) if ...; or (b) if ..." deems a case and says nothing of the books that meet both limbs (fork F-396B-3; marginal reading (a) is the other reading)
    WHERE
        necessaryBooksKept MEANS
                `books or accounts necessary to exhibit and explain the transactions and financial position of the trade or business of the company have been kept`
            AND `books containing entries from day to day in sufficient detail of all cash received and cash paid have been kept`
            AND (   (NOT `the trade or business has involved dealings in goods`)
                 OR (`statements of the annual stocktakings have been kept` AND (`the goods were sold by way of ordinary retail trade` OR `statements of all goods sold and purchased, showing the goods and the buyers and sellers in sufficient detail to enable them to be identified, have been kept`)))
        auditable MEANS `the books or accounts have been kept in such manner as to enable them to be conveniently and properly audited`

§ `Section 397: translations`

DECLARE `s 397 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 397(1) lodge at the same time with the Registrar a certified translation in the English language`
    `s 397(2) keep at the registered office in Singapore a certified translation in the English language`
    `s 397(3) cause a true translation of the accounts, financial statements, minute books and other records to be made`

-- src:27778 | 397.—(1) Where under this Act a corporation is required to lodge
-- src:27779 | with the Registrar any instrument, certificate, contract or document or
-- src:27780 | a certified copy thereof and the same is not written in the English
-- src:27785 | language, the corporation must lodge at the same time with the
-- src:27786 | Registrar a certified translation thereof in the English language.
@ref s 397(1) (src:27778-27786)
GIVEN `the corporation is required under this Act to lodge with the Registrar the instrument, certificate, contract or document or a certified copy of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is not written in the English language` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has lodged at the same time with the Registrar a certified translation in the English language` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 397(1) the corporation has lodged the certified translation that the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the corporation is required under this Act to lodge with the Registrar the instrument, certificate, contract or document or a certified copy of it` AND `the document is not written in the English language`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where under this Act a corporation is required to lodge with the Registrar any instrument ... and the same is not written in the English language" (fork F-397-1: a duty whose "where" is unmet)
    ELSE (IF `the corporation has lodged at the same time with the Registrar a certified translation in the English language`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the corporation must lodge at the same time with the Registrar a certified translation thereof in the English language" (a duty)

@ref s 397(1) (src:27778-27786)
GIVEN `the name of the corporation` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 397 act`
`s 397(1) a corporation must lodge a certified English translation at the same time` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the corporation`
    MUST `s 397(1) lodge at the same time with the Registrar a certified translation in the English language`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:27788 | (2) Where under this Act a corporation is required to make
-- src:27789 | available for public inspection any instrument, certificate, contract
-- src:27790 | or document and the same is not written in the English language, the
-- src:27791 | corporation must keep at its registered office in Singapore a certified
-- src:27792 | translation thereof in the English language.
@ref s 397(2) (src:27788-27792)
GIVEN `the corporation is required under this Act to make available for public inspection the instrument, certificate, contract or document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is not written in the English language` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation keeps at its registered office in Singapore a certified translation in the English language` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 397(2) the corporation has kept the certified translation that the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the corporation is required under this Act to make available for public inspection the instrument, certificate, contract or document` AND `the document is not written in the English language`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where under this Act a corporation is required to make available for public inspection any instrument ... and the same is not written in the English language" (fork F-397-1)
    ELSE (IF `the corporation keeps at its registered office in Singapore a certified translation in the English language`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the corporation must keep at its registered office in Singapore a certified translation thereof in the English language" (a duty)

@ref s 397(2) (src:27788-27792)
GIVEN `the name of the corporation` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 397 act`
`s 397(2) a corporation must keep a certified English translation at its registered office` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the corporation`
    MUST `s 397(2) keep at the registered office in Singapore a certified translation in the English language`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- (3): "at intervals of not more than 7 days": the next true translation is made not later than 7 days after the last (sg-periods P2, "not later than").
-- src:27794 | (3) Where any accounts, financial statements, minute books or
-- src:27795 | other records of a corporation required by this Act to be kept are not
-- src:27796 | kept in the English language, the directors of the corporation must
-- src:27797 | cause a true translation of such accounts, financial statements, minute
-- src:27798 | books and other records to be made from time to time at intervals of
-- src:27799 | not more than 7 days and must cause such translations to be kept with
-- src:27800 | the original accounts, financial statements, minute books and other
-- src:27801 | records for so long as the original accounts, financial statements,
-- src:27802 | minute books and other records are required by this Act to be kept.
@ref s 397(3) (src:27794-27802)
GIVEN `the records of the corporation required by this Act to be kept are not kept in the English language` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the last true translation was made` IS A DATE
      `the day the next true translation is made` IS A DATE
      `the translations are kept with the original records for so long as the original records are required by this Act to be kept` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 397(3) the directors have caused the true translations to be made and kept as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `the records of the corporation required by this Act to be kept are not kept in the English language`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where any accounts, financial statements, minute books or other records of a corporation required by this Act to be kept are not kept in the English language" (fork F-397-1)
    ELSE (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the last true translation was made` `the day the next true translation is made` 7 Days AND `the translations are kept with the original records for so long as the original records are required by this Act to be kept`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the directors of the corporation must cause a true translation ... to be made from time to time at intervals of not more than 7 days and must cause such translations to be kept with the original" (a duty)

@ref s 397(3) (src:27794-27802)
GIVEN `the name of the corporation` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 397 act`
`s 397(3) the directors must cause a true translation to be made within 7 days of the last` MEANS
    PARTY `Board of directors` `the name of the corporation`
    MUST `s 397(3) cause a true translation of the accounts, financial statements, minute books and other records to be made`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `Board of directors` `the name of the corporation` BECAUSE "no true translation was made within 7 days of the last"

§ `Section 398: certificate of incorporation conclusive evidence`

DECLARE `s 398 document` IS ONE OF
    `s 398 a certificate of incorporation under the hand and seal of the Registrar issued under this Act in force before 13 January 2003`
    `s 398 a notice of incorporation issued by the Registrar under this Act`
    `s 398 a certificate of confirmation of incorporation of the Registrar issued under this Act`
    `s 398 some other document`

-- src:27808 | 398. A certificate of incorporation under the hand and seal of the
-- src:27809 | Registrar issued under this Act in force before 13 January 2003, a
-- src:27810 | notice of incorporation issued by the Registrar under this Act, and a
-- src:27811 | certificate of confirmation of incorporation of the Registrar issued
-- src:27812 | under this Act, are each conclusive evidence that all the requirements
-- src:27813 | of this Act in respect of registration and of matters precedent and
-- src:27814 | incidental thereto have been complied with, and that the company
-- src:27815 | referred to therein is duly incorporated under this Act.
@ref s 398 (src:27808-27815)
GIVEN document IS A `s 398 document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 398 the document is conclusive evidence that the requirements of this Act in respect of registration have been complied with and that the company is duly incorporated under this Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `s 398 a certificate of incorporation under the hand and seal of the Registrar issued under this Act in force before 13 January 2003` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 398 a notice of incorporation issued by the Registrar under this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 398 a certificate of confirmation of incorporation of the Registrar issued under this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "A certificate ..., a notice ..., and a certificate of confirmation ... are each conclusive evidence" names three documents and does not say "only"
